# 000700-000799/20130620T181352Z_560782907.wiki
zΔ⚡b|=558b|-ae|=479|+%0A%0A'''spiff''' compares [[Computer file%7Cfile]]s' logical not literal differences thus the same as diff but ignoring differences in:%0A# floating point calculations with roundoff errors<ref name%3D"dontcallme">{{cite%2Dweb%7Curl%3Dhttps://github.com/dontcallmedom/spiff%7Ctitle%3Dspiff%7Cauthor%3Ddontcallmedotcom%7Caccessdate%3D2013%2D06%2D16}}</ref><ref>{{cite%2Dweb%7Curl%3Dhttp://stackoverflow.com/a/1489107/2291035%7Cdate%3D2009%2D09%2D28%7Cauthor%3DDavide%7Ctitle%3Dstackoverflow%7Caccessdate%3D2013%2D06%2D16}}</ref><ref name%3D"hpux">{{cite%2Dweb%7Curl%3Dhttp://hpux.connect.org.uk/hppd/hpux/Text/spiff%2D1.0/%7Ctitle%3DHP%2DUX Porting and Archiving%7Clocation%3DUK%7Cfirst%3DDaniel W%7Clast%3DNachbar%7Cdate%3D1999%2D12%2D01%7Caccessdate%3D2013%2D06%2D13}}</ref>%0A# and [[Space (punctuation)%7Cwhitespace]]<ref name%3D"dontcallme"/><ref name%3D"hpux"/>%0Awhich are generally irrelevant to source code comparison. An extreme inverse is [[cmp (Unix)%7Ccmp]]. [[Telcordia Technologies%7CBellcore]] wrote the original version<ref name%3D"dontcallme"/><ref name%3D"hpux"/>. An [[HPUX]] port is the most current public release. spiff does not support binary files<ref>{{cite%2Dweb%7Curl%3Dhttp://www.math.utah.edu/cgi%2Dbin/man2html.cgi?/usr/local/man/man1/spiff.1%7Ctitle%3DSPIFF 1%7Cdate%3D1988%2D02%2D02%7Caccessdate%3D2013%2D06%2D16}}</ref><ref>{{cite%2Dweb%7Curl%3Dhttp://hpux.connect.org.uk/hppd/hpux/Text/spiff%2D1.0/man.html%7Ctitle%3DMan page%7Clocation%3DUK%7Cfirst%3DDaniel W%7Clast%3DNachbar%7Cdate%3D1988%2D02%2D02%7Caccessdate%3D2013%2D06%2D16}}</ref>. spiff outputs to the [[standard output]] in standard diff format and accepts inputs in the [[C (programming language)%7CC]], [[Bourne shell]], [[Fortran]], [[Modula%2D2]] and [[Lisp (programming language)%7CLisp]] [[programming language]]s.|=8b8|
