zΔ⚡b|=1c30|+Usage %3D%3D%0A%0AThe <tt>diff</tt> command is invoked from the command line, passing it the names of two files: <tt>diff ''original'' ''new''</tt>. The output of the command represents the changes required to transform the ''original'' file into the ''new'' file.%0A%0AIf ''original'' and ''new'' are directories, then <tt>diff</tt> will be run on each file that exists in both directories. An option, <tt>%2Dr</tt>, will recursively descend any matching subdirectories to compare files between directories.%0A%0AAny of the examples in the article use the following two files, ''original'' and ''new'':%0A{{Col%2Dbegin}}%0A{{Col%2Dbreak%7Cwidth%3D33%25}}%0A''original'':%0A<source lang%3D"text" line>%0AThis part of the%0Adocument has stayed the%0Asame from version to%0Aversion.  It shouldn't%0Abe shown if it doesn't%0Achange.  Otherwise, that%0Awould not be helping to%0Acompress the size of the%0Achanges.%0A%0AThis paragraph contains%0Atext that is outdated.%0AIt will be deleted in the%0Anear future.%0A%0AIt is important to spell%0Acheck this dokument. On%0Athe other hand, a%0Amisspelled word isn't%0Athe end of the world.%0ANothing in the rest of%0Athis paragraph needs to%0Abe changed. Things can%0Abe added after it.%0A</source>%0A{{col%2Dbreak}}%0A''new'':%0A<source lang%3D"text" line>%0AThis is an important%0Anotice! It should%0Atherefore be located at%0Athe beginning of this%0Adocument!%0A%0AThis part of the%0Adocument has stayed the%0Asame from version to%0Aversion.  It shouldn't%0Abe shown if it doesn't%0Achange.  Otherwise, that%0Awould not be helping to%0Acompress anything.%0A%0AIt is important to spell%0Acheck this document. On%0Athe other hand, a%0Amisspelled word isn't%0Athe end of the world.%0ANothing in the rest of%0Athis paragraph needs to%0Abe changed. Things can%0Abe added after it.%0A%0AThis paragraph contains%0Aimportant new additions%0Ato this document.%0A</source>%0A{{col%2Dbreak%7Cwidth%3D33%25}}%0AThe command '''<tt>diff original new</tt>''' produces the following ''normal diff output'':%0A{{pre%7C%0A0a1,6%0A{{font color%7Cdarkgreen%7C> This is an important%0A> notice! It should%0A> therefore be located at%0A> the beginning of this%0A> document!%0A>}}%0A8,14c14%0A{{font color%7Cdarkred%7C< compress the size of the%0A< changes.%0A<%0A< This paragraph contains%0A< text that is outdated.%0A< It will be deleted in the%0A< near future.}}%0A%2D%2D%2D%0A{{font color%7Cdarkgreen%7C> compress anything.}}%0A17c17%0A{{font color%7Cdarkred%7C< check this dokument. On}}%0A%2D%2D%2D%0A{{font color%7Cdarkgreen%7C> check this document. On}}%0A24a25,28%0A{{font color%7Cdarkgreen%7C>%0A> This paragraph contains%0A> important new additions%0A> to this document.}}}}%0A%0A{{Note2}} ''Here, the diff output is shown with colors to make it easier to read. The diff utility does not produce colored output; its output is [[plain text]]. However, many tools can show the output with colors by using [[syntax highlighting]].''%0A{{col%2Dend}}%0AIn this traditional output format, '''<tt>a</tt>''' stands for ''added'', '''<tt>d</tt>''' for ''deleted'' and '''<tt>c</tt>''' for ''changed''. Line numbers of the original file appear before <tt>a</tt>/<tt>d</tt>/<tt>c</tt> and those of the modified file appear after. The [[Less%2Dthan sign%7Cless%2Dthan]] and [[Greater%2Dthan sign%7Cgreater%2Dthan]] signs (at the beginning of lines that are added, deleted or changed) indicate which file the lines appear in. Addition lines are added to the original file to appear in the new file. Deletion lines are deleted from the original file to be missing in the new file.%0A%0ABy default, lines common to both files are not shown. Lines that have moved are shown as added at their new location and as deleted from their old location.<ref>{{cite book%7Ctitle%3DComparing and Merging Files with GNU Diff and Patch%7Curl%3Dhttps://www.gnu.org/software/diffutils/manual/%7Cauthor1%3DDavid MacKenzie %7Cauthor2%3DPaul Eggert %7Cauthor3%3DRichard Stallman %7Cisbn%3D0%2D9541617%2D5%2D0%7Cpublisher%3DNetwork Theory%7Cyear%3D1997%7Clocation%3DBristol}}</ref> However, some diff tools highlight moved lines.%0A%0A%3D%3D |=44cb|
